T0.4: HTTPS transport support for shared test libraries
Date: 2026-05-15

=== bash -n syntax validation ===
transport.sh:   PASS
load_env.sh:    PASS
restart_bridge.sh: PASS

=== transport.sh changes ===
- Added BRIDGE_PORT, BRIDGE_HTTPS_URL, BRIDGE_HTTPS_MODE, BRIDGE_CURL_INSECURE exports
- detect_transport(): step 5 tries HTTPS first (curl -ksSf), step 6 falls back to HTTP
- When HTTPS succeeds: BRIDGE_HTTP_URL overridden to HTTPS URL, BRIDGE_CURL_INSECURE="-k"
- rpc_call() and rpc_call_auth(): curl calls now include ${BRIDGE_CURL_INSECURE} flag
- Function signatures unchanged: rpc_call, rpc_call_auth, detect_transport, require_bridge, optional_bridge

=== load_env.sh changes ===
- check_bridge_running(): tries curl -ksSf HTTPS first, falls back to HTTP

=== restart_bridge.sh changes ===
- _bridge_is_local(): tries HTTPS first, falls back to HTTP
- Local health polling: tries HTTPS first, falls back to HTTP
- Remote health polling (ssh_vps): tries HTTPS first, falls back to HTTP
